  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 142 AM CDT Sun Oct 18 2026\n\nToday looks to be the coolest of the next 7 days with highs in\nthe low to mid 60s. Monday onward high temperatures should be in\nthe upper 60s or 70s each day. No precipitation is expected the\nnext 7+ days with cloudless or nearly cloudless skies many of \nthe days. Gusty southwest winds will develop this afternoon in \nresponse to a tightening pressure gradient from deep low \npressure tracking across central Canada. In the wake of that \nsystem sfc high pressure will become established over the upper \nGreat Lakes/southeast Canada resulting in lighter winds much of \nthe upcoming work week. Weak afternoon lake breezes could bring \nsome modest cooling near the lake in the afternoons. A peek \nbeyond day 7 of the forecast suggests that this pattern could \npersist the rest of October.\n\n- Izzi",
